      "writtenOn": "2026-11-20T08:53:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When write() fails (written \u003c 0) this logs \"wrote -1\" with no errno, so a genuine write error and a short write look alike, and the failure reason is lost. The byte-write path in writeFRU() already logs strerror(errno).\n\nCould the written \u003c 0 case log strerror(errno) (captured before the lg2 call), and keep the expected/actual form only for short writes?",
      "revId": "713518c44ca80dc13aaef2a6ae4501115584baff",
